# A loop that holds its elements against numbers asks its list for storage of numbers first. A switch over an element is such a holding too, but there the raw number has to be made an integer again
# for the switch: an instruction an element more than switching on the boxed value. So where the elements are switched on the list has its one copy as before; where they are compared it is asked.
# f1 = weigh, f2 = count
